 1080 "Ae^{-6x}+2x+1" 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409488 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409488 1083 #uuid "a813be27-9e89-5447-a6ed-ccb753aec0ff" 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409489 1080 "-2x+1" 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409489 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409489 1083 #uuid "fcf2db36-4823-5f0f-a979-18eb641ef853" 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409490 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409486 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409490 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409490 1077 "field-1" 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409490 1078 #edb/ref 17592186409486 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409490 1079 #uuid "8e554faf-bf14-5f8b-8095-42b409f87077" 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409491 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409487 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409491 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409491 1077 "field-1" 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409491 1078 #edb/ref 17592186409487 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409491 1079 #uuid "e5c92c86-227c-5c65-bc14-31ff63640148" 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409492 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409488 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409492 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409492 1077 "field-1" 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409492 1078 #edb/ref 17592186409488 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409492 1079 #uuid "ea7da04c-6c47-53af-93ba-6b58aa8bcba5" 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409493 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409489 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409493 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409493 1077 "field-1" 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409493 1078 #edb/ref 17592186409489 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409493 1079 #uuid "fc1fdf7c-1bca-53aa-87e0-8b914a783aff" 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409494 1068 #edb/ref 17592186409493 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409494 1069 "q-332303" 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409494 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409494 1071 "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-6y=12x-8.\n$$\n\nFind the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation.\n\n${y}_{p}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409494 1072 #uuid "11008462-bb8d-5c30-9ab6-4b789c8f149b" 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409494 1074 "The right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is a polynomial of degree $1.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also a polynomial of degree $1,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha x+\\beta \n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=\\alpha .\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\alpha -6(\\alpha x+\\beta )=12x-8\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n-6\\alpha x+(\\alpha -6\\beta )=12x-8.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-6\\alpha =12\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,x) \\\\ \\alpha -6\\beta =-8\\, & (\\text{equating the constants})\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-2,\\,\\beta =1.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-2x+1.\n$$" 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409495 1068 #edb/ref 17592186409490 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409495 1069 "q-332544" 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409495 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409495 1071 "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y=-8.\n$$\n\nFind the general solution to this equation given that the complementary solution is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-4x},$ where $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409495 1072 #uuid "927f3245-f67b-58d6-852d-475c4b37e55f" 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409495 1074 "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{c}}{\\text{d}x}+4{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{-4x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is a polynomial of degree $0.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also a polynomial of degree $0,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\beta \n$$\n\nwhere $\\beta $ is a constant to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=0.\n$$\n\nTo find the value of $\\beta ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n0+4\\beta =-8\n$$\n\nSolving this equation gives $\\beta =-2.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-2.\n$$\n\nNow, since the general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nthe general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-4x}-2.\n$$" 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409496 1068 #edb/ref 17592186409491 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409496 1069 "q-332291" 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409496 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409496 1071 "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}-4y=8.\n$$\n\nFind the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation.\n\n${y}_{p}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409496 1072 #uuid "abc3945b-d976-54fe-bc38-a631f9c8a6c5" 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409496 1074 "The right-hand side of our inhomogeneous equation is a polynomial of degree $0.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also a polynomial of degree $0,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha ,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ is a constant to be determined.\n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}^{′}(x)=0.\n$$\n\nTo find the value of $\\alpha ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n0-4\\alpha =8\\,⟹\\,\\alpha =-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-2.\n$$" 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409497 1058 #edb/ref 17592186409498 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409497 1062 #uuid "19ee83f6-1de2-5260-a0ac-12e506110b20" 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409497 1063 #edb/ref 17592186409495 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409498 1062 #uuid "218a75cb-ded3-56d6-8e5a-f6b0268721ec" 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409498 1063 #edb/ref 17592186308362 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409499 1058 #edb/ref 17592186409497 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409499 1062 #uuid "2c1d4d31-bdd3-5e06-8ac4-128b5af0e137" 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409499 1063 #edb/ref 17592186363726 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409500 1058 #edb/ref 17592186409501 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409500 1062 #uuid "5fac2716-ce9b-5cad-acde-41963ce110a0" 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [17592186409500 1063 #edb/ref 17592186409496 13194139533571 17592186045417 true] [175921